  "agent": "holmes-mcp",
  "artifact_text": "**Observations**\n- Pod `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf` logs report `WARN db connection reset by peer, retrying (pool acquire 2.80s)`.\n- Metric `http_requests_total{service=\"billing-api\",status=\"504\"}` shows active 504 errors while `app_heap_bytes` remains bounded.\n- The `DBProxy` resource `billing-db-proxy` sets `idleClientTimeout: 600`, whereas the `billing-api` Deployment configures `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS: 900`.\n\n**Ruled-out leads**\n- Application memory leak ruled out because heap growth is an artifact of stalled requests as documented in INC-2024-0312 and RB-014.\n- Pod crash/OOMKill ruled out because the pod status is Running with 0 restarts and probes passing.\n\n**Root cause**\nThe RDS DBProxy `idleClientTimeout` (600s) is shorter than the application database pool idle recycling timeout (900s), causing the proxy to drop connections before the client recycles them.\n\n**Recommended action**\nThe platform team should update `DBProxy/billing-db-proxy` to remove or increase `idleClientTimeout` above 900s (e.g., AWS default 1800s), or the billing team should lower `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` below 600s.",
